// Test: bugfixes/codegen_string_accum_non_empty_init_leak
// Grammar: variable_declaration, while_statement, binary_expression
// Semantic: CODEGEN-STRING-ACCUM-NON-EMPTY-INIT-LEAK
//
// Regression pin for dashboard fingerprint 6fca1073d4bd (reported against
// 0.33.61).
//
// The HIR single-accumulator rewrite (rewrite_string_accumulator_loops in
// src/hir/hir_builder.rs) only fires when the accumulator is declared as
// `string acc = ""` — an empty-literal initializer. When the initializer
// is any other string literal (e.g. `string result = "["`), the whole
// pipeline (string_builder_new + string_builder_append + finalize +
// transient-scope wrap) is skipped and every `result = result + ...` in
// the loop body stays on the raw string.concat path. Each concat
// __malloc's a fresh block on the main heap and orphans the previous
// `result`, giving O(N²) main-heap growth. At 500 iterations with
// ~30-byte fragments this traps at the linear memory boundary on the
// standalone runner.
//
// Fix: seed the builder with the initial literal as a single
// string_builder_append(__sb_N, <init literal>) call right after
// string_builder_new, mirroring the shape apply_dual_scope_rewrite
// already uses for non-empty A/B seeds.
//
// Body has exactly one self-append on `result` (the accumulator-rewrite
// predicate `analysis.is_rewritable()` requires self_appends == 1). The
// RHS is a pure string literal so this test isolates the non-empty-init
// leak from unrelated per-iter heap allocations (e.g. `k.toString()`
// bridge returns).
//
// Total length: 1 (`[`) + 3000 * len(",") + 1 (`]`) = 3002.
//
// Pre-fix (0.33.63 and earlier): the accumulator rewrite predicate
// `accumulator_decl_name` in src/hir/hir_builder.rs required the
// initializer to be `""`; `string result = "["` failed the predicate and
// the whole pipeline (string_builder_new + string_builder_append +
// finalize + transient-scope wrap) was skipped. Every
// `result = result + ","` in the loop stayed on the raw string.concat
// path, __malloc-ing a fresh block on the main heap and orphaning the
// prior `result`. At 3000 iterations wasmtime's linear-memory grew
// unboundedly and emitted `memory.grow failed for 1 pages` thousands of
// times before the pass completed (or trapped, on tighter runners like
// clean-server).
//
// Post-fix (0.33.64+): `accumulator_decl_name` accepts any string
// literal, `try_match_accumulator_pair` seeds the builder with a single
// `__sb_N = string_builder_append(__sb_N, "[")` right after
// `string_builder_new`, and every subsequent self-append routes through
// host-arena bump inside the transient scope. Main-heap growth is
// bounded, `memory.grow failed` no longer fires, and the finalized
// string length is exactly 3002.
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.64
// Expected output:
//   3002

start:
	string blob = build_array(3000)
	printl(blob.length().toString())

functions:
	string build_array(integer n)
		string result = "["
		integer k = 0
		while k < n
			result = result + ","
			k = k + 1
		result = result + "]"
		return result
